  "evaluation": "All three correctly classify the disagreement as genuine, identify population as the primary reason, and list outcome measurement and design as secondary differences. Both studies concern vitamin D and depressive symptoms, and neither provides an explicit underpowering signal or confidence interval that dissolves the disagreement. A ranks first for its specific description of the populations and exposure contrasts. B closely follows, usefully noting Study B's adjusted null finding. C is also correct but provides less supporting detail.",
